# CLOSURE (qa-pr1195-r1, quality-mgr): arch-ctm's fix (57bedb0ce, PR #1195 ->
# integrate/phase-aw) removes the PausedTimeline mock entirely
# (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs, -95 lines,
# including ac7_offer_overflow_counts_the_paused_writer_excess) and replaces
# it with ac7_real_diagnostic_channel_saturation_persists_a_bridged_row_after_drain
# (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/mod.rs:1097). quality-mgr
# independently confirmed in /tmp/verify-aw2-i2 at 57bedb0ce: the new test
# fills the real bounded tokio::sync::mpsc diagnostic channel
# (DIAGNOSTIC_QUEUE_BATCHES capacity) via try_send to a real
# TrySendError::Full, then drives the real production selector
# receive_next_work (writer/mod.rs:564) to pull the first batch, calls the
# real process_diagnostic_batch, and asserts the bridged
# ATM_BRIDGED_FIXTURE/tracing row is persisted via a real
# `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM diagnostic_events` against SQLite -- this closes the
# AC7 gap this finding was narrowed to (bridged-row-persists-to-SQLite under
# real channel saturation), not a mock. cargo test -p atm-storage-rusqlite -p
# atm-daemon-bootstrap: 134 passed, 0 failed, no regressions (includes
# ac3_primary_mailbox_insert_completes_while_diagnostic_lane_is_full from
# ATM-QA-AW2R9-001, still green alongside the new AC7 test). PR #1195 ->
# integrate/phase-aw: required lint/clippy/format/hermes-wheel checks green;
# Test (ubuntu/macos/windows-latest) and Just lint (macos/windows) still
# IN_PROGRESS at review time -- CI is a merge gate only, not a QA-dispatch
# gate, per standing merge policy; will flag if any of those come back red.
# Forward-merged into feature/aw3-health-and-log-query @ 9be864e350a per
# arch-ctm's notice, no separate re-verification needed there since it is a
# clean fast-forward of the same commit onto an unrelated branch.

# UPDATE (qa-pr1179-r9, quality-mgr): req-qa's round-9 full-AC audit (filed
# as ATM-QA-AW2R9-002) independently confirmed the AC7 gap remains: the
# PausedTimeline mock (diagnostic_timeline.rs:423-445) manufactures a canned
# "queue is full" error after N accepted calls via
# atm_runtime_test_support::diagnostic_queue_batches_for_test() rather than
# exercising the real bounded tokio::sync::mpsc channel that lives in
# crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/mod.rs. quality-mgr independently
# read the mock's implementation and confirms this characterization. Status
# stays open/important; superseded in tracking terms by ATM-QA-AW2R9-002 but
# this record is retained per append-only convention.

# PARTIAL FIX (qa-pr1179-r8, quality-mgr): AW.2 round-8 (fee01b959) added
# ac2_policy_selected_info_rows_reach_the_timeline,
# ac3_diagnostic_persistence_failure_does_not_poison_later_offers
# (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs), and
# ac4_prune_reduces_a_25k_fixture_to_the_documented_row_bound
# (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs), all independently
# confirmed genuine by quality-mgr, req-qa, and rust-qa-agent -- these close
# the AC2/AC3/AC4 portion of this finding. AC7's new test,
# ac7_saturation_state_transitions_from_degraded_to_recovered_after_quiet_window
# (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:496), only drives
# DegradationMonitor::observe() directly with a manually backdated
# degraded_since; it never exercises DiagnosticTimelineWriter::offer under a
# real paused-writer/queue-full scenario, and asserts no
# timeline_dropped_queue_full_total-equals-excess or single-emission
# guarantee. Confirmed independently by quality-mgr and req-qa (filed as
# req-qa's ATM-QA-AW2R8-001, Important); rust-qa-agent's pass did not flag
# this gap and does not overrule the two independent confirmations. This
# finding is narrowed to the remaining AC7 gap; status stays open/important.

